body:
@fserb I did a pass through to fix up the various issues I found. Please look at the commit message on my latest push for details.

For most they were editorial, or the fix was straightforward. But the one that was really puzzling were the changes you made to "run the animation frame callbacks", which I didn't understand the reasoning for. I reverted them because they seemed likely to be wrong, but I'd love to understand what the thinking was there.

Please take a look at my changes and make sure they're aligned with what you had in mind :).

@wanderview I think currently the spec is trying to leave framerate, background throttling, etc. up to UAs, both for the window and worker cases. Are you asking about Chrome's planned implementation?
